# /etc/sudoers.d/sigmond-fleet-readonly
#
# Install with:
#     install -m 0440 -o root -g root \
#         etc/sudoers.d/sigmond-fleet-readonly /etc/sudoers.d/
#     visudo -c            # MUST pass before you log out
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
#
# `smd fleet doctor` and `smd fleet update` connect to each host as the
# `sigmond` user. Two read-only checks need root and degrade honestly
# without it, reporting less rather than reporting wrongly:
#
#   * exec-mismatch reads /proc/<pid>/exe to confirm a running service
#     executes the binary its deploy tree provides. That link is
#     unreadable for another user's process, so as `sigmond` every
#     service came back `running=(unreadable) status=unknown`.
#
#   * `smd update` refreshes origin/* before deciding a host is current.
#     `_git_fetch_as_owner` DROPS privileges to each repo's owner — which
#     it can only do if it has privileges to drop. As `sigmond` it cannot
#     fetch a timestd-owned checkout, so that ref stays stale: hf-timestd
#     sat 19 commits behind on DASI002 and `smd update` reported the host
#     current.
#
# WHY IT IS SCOPED THIS WAY
#
# sudo matches the command AND its arguments exactly. Listing `smd
# doctor` with no arguments therefore permits ONLY the bare, read-only
# invocation:
#
#     sudo -n smd doctor          permitted
#     sudo -n smd doctor --fix    REFUSED (prompts for a password)
#     sudo -n smd update          permitted
#     sudo -n smd update --apply  REFUSED (prompts for a password)
#
# So the fan-out can report on every host without ever being able to
# change one. Rolling the fleet forward stays a deliberate, interactive
# act.
#
# Two narrower-looking alternatives were rejected:
#
#   * `NOPASSWD: /bin/readlink /proc/*/exe` cannot work at all — smd
#     reads that link with an in-process os.readlink() syscall
#     (bin/smd, _resolve_exe), which no sudoers rule can affect.
#
#   * `NOPASSWD: (timestd, wsprrec, ...) /usr/bin/git` is far BROADER
#     than it looks. git as another user is near-total impersonation of
#     them: hooks, aliases, --exec-path, -c core.pager=<anything>.
#
# SAFETY NOTE
#
# `smd doctor` run as root does NOT recreate the root-owned .git damage
# it exists to detect: sigmond.doctor.git_state passes
# --no-optional-locks precisely so `git status` cannot rewrite
# .git/index. See the comment there — that damage was observed on
# DASI002 and is why the flag is present.
#
# The trailing full paths matter: a bare `smd` would let any binary
# named smd earlier in PATH be run as root.

Cmnd_Alias SIGMOND_FLEET_RO = /usr/local/bin/smd doctor, \
                              /usr/local/bin/smd update, \
                              /usr/local/bin/smd version

sigmond ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: SIGMOND_FLEET_RO
